\section{Hybrid Stability Across Live Reconfiguration}
\label{sec:hybrid-live-stability}

Normal Live intervals use the source-word funnel certificate of
Theorem~\ref{thm:widen-path-direct-iss}.  Hard attitude/reference events are
explicit jumps
\begin{equation}
 (\vct e^+,\pi^+)=\mathcal R_j(\vct e^-,\pi^-;\mu_j),
 \qquad j\in\{M,T\},
 \label{eq:hybrid-jump-map}
\end{equation}
where $M$ denotes magnetic-gauge acquisition/refinement and $T$ a tilt re-lock.
A jump is certified by its exact image, its destination source-node metric, and
the same scalar funnel recursion used for normal source words.

\subsection{Magnetic-gauge jump}
\label{sec:hybrid-mag-jump}

The source-realizable magnetic family contains the first Live gauge acquisition
when Live began without north and the one-time refined magnetic reference.  Let
$\rho_M\in\{0,1\}$ identify the two events.  When a finite acquired yaw
$\psi_M$ is available, the nominal attitude operation is
\begin{equation}
 q^+_{bw}=R_z(\psi_M)\,\mathcal Q_{\rm tilt}(q^-_{bw}),
 \label{eq:hybrid-mag-attitude-map}
\end{equation}
while $(b_g,v,p,S,a_w,b_a)$ are numerically unchanged.  The associated source
flags, magnetic reference, hard-iron state, and possible bias-enable covariance
floor are included in the bounded mode map
$\pi^+=\mathcal P_M(\pi^-,\rho_M)$.

Let the adopted horizontal gauge change by
\begin{equation}
 \Delta\psi_M=b_{\psi,\mathrm{ref}}^+-b_{\psi,\mathrm{ref}}^-,
 \qquad \mat Q_M=R_z(\Delta\psi_M).
 \label{eq:hybrid-mag-gauge-change}
\end{equation}
The gauge-referenced physical vectors satisfy $x_g^+=\mat Q_Mx_g^-$ for
$x\in\{v,p,S,a_w\}$.  Since the stored additive nominal states are not rotated,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \vct e_x^+=\vct e_x^-+(\mat I-\mat Q_M)\vct x_g^- .}
 \label{eq:hybrid-mag-world-error-jump}
\end{equation}
Assume
\begin{equation}
 |\Delta\psi_M|\le\bar\Delta_M<\pi,
 \qquad
 |\delta\psi_{\rm int}^+|\le\bar\epsilon_M,
 \label{eq:hybrid-mag-heading-residual}
\end{equation}
and bounded physical world-vector magnitudes
$\|x_g^-\|\le\bar X_M$.  Then
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \|\vct e_x^+\|
 \le\|\vct e_x^-\|
 +2\sin(\bar\Delta_M/2)\bar X_M.}
 \label{eq:hybrid-mag-world-error-bound}
\end{equation}

For any compact pre-jump funnel section $X\subset\mathcal D_i$, define the
exact magnetic jump image
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathfrak J_M(X):=
 \{\mathcal R_M(\vct e,\pi;\mu_M,\rho_M):
 \vct e\in X,\ \pi\in\Pi_M,\ \mu_M\in\mathcal M_M,
 \ \rho_M\in\{0,1\}\}.}
 \label{eq:hybrid-mag-envelope}
\end{equation}
The family is compact under the declared heading and physical-state bounds.
Each magnetic event occurs at most once.  Continuous hard-iron correction after
refinement is part of the normal source-word family rather than a hard jump.

\subsection{Tilt re-lock jump}
\label{sec:hybrid-tilt-jump}

The Live tilt re-lock uses the source map
\begin{equation}
 q^+_{bw}=R_z(\psi^-_{E})Q_y(\vartheta_a)Q_x(\varphi_a),
 \label{eq:hybrid-tilt-attitude-map}
\end{equation}
where $\psi^-_E$ is the pre-reset ZYX Euler yaw and
$(\varphi_a,\vartheta_a)$ are reconstructed from the current accelerometer.
All additive nominal states are unchanged.  The attitude covariance is reseeded
and its cross-covariances are cleared by the implemented reset map.

A deterministic tilt bound requires
\begin{equation}
 \vct f_b=-g\vct u_d+\vct\epsilon_f,
 \qquad \|\vct\epsilon_f\|\le\bar f_T<g.
 \label{eq:hybrid-tilt-force-bound}
\end{equation}
Then tangent-ball geometry gives
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \|\delta\vct\theta_\perp^+\|
 \le\bar\theta_T:=\sin^{-1}(\bar f_T/g)<\frac{\pi}{2}.}
 \label{eq:hybrid-tilt-reset-bound}
\end{equation}
The reset trigger alone is not a substitute for this physical force bound.

Because the source preserves ZYX Euler yaw, admit the compact chart
\begin{equation}
 |\cos\vartheta^-|\ge c_\psi>0,
 \qquad |\cos\vartheta_g|\ge c_\psi>0.
 \label{eq:hybrid-tilt-yaw-chart}
\end{equation}
On this chart
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\epsilon_{\psi,E}^+=\epsilon_{\psi,E}^-,}
 \label{eq:hybrid-tilt-yaw-preserved}
\end{equation}
and smooth coordinate equivalence gives a finite post-reset local-yaw bound.
Let $\mathfrak J_T(X)$ denote the exact compact image of the admissible re-lock
guard subset of $X$ under this source map.

The source cooldown supplies the dwell-time bound
\begin{equation}
 T_{\rm cool}=3\ \mathrm{s},
 \qquad
 N_{\rm cool}:=\left\lceil\frac{T_{\rm cool}}{h_+}\right\rceil
 \label{eq:hybrid-tilt-dwell}
\end{equation}
between completed tilt re-locks.  Recurrent-reset small gain is derived once,
in Sec.~\ref{sec:stability-widening-phase-e}, from this exact reset and the
source-word cooldown contraction.

\subsection{Exact jump-to-funnel certification}

Consider an admissible jump from source node $i$ to node $j$.  For a pre-jump
funnel section $\mathcal F_i(c_i)$, require
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathfrak J_j(\mathcal F_i(c_i))\subseteq\mathcal D_j,
 \qquad
 W_j(\mathcal R_j(e,\pi;\mu_j))
 \le\lambda_{J,j}W_i(e)+\gamma_{J,j}(\bar d),}
 \label{eq:hybrid-jump-entry}
\end{equation}
for every admitted pre-jump state, source mode, and jump datum, with finite
$\lambda_{J,j}\ge0$.  The post-jump level is inserted directly into the funnel
recursion of Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-funnel-recursion}.  Subsequent normal-Live
words obey Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-funnel-word}, and every word prefix remains in
its source-node proof domain.

\begin{theorem}[Hybrid Live jump-to-funnel recovery]
\label{thm:hybrid-live-recovery}
Assume normal-Live intervals satisfy
Theorem~\ref{thm:widen-path-direct-iss}; every magnetic or tilt jump satisfies
Eq.~\eqref{eq:hybrid-jump-entry}; and every post-jump source word has certified
prefix safety.  Then every finite source-realizable sequence of hard jumps
remains in the source-funnel domain and, after its final jump, obeys the same
regional practical-ISS funnel bound as normal Live.  The positive source
cooldown excludes Zeno accumulation of tilt re-locks.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Equation~\eqref{eq:hybrid-jump-entry} maps each hard event into a certified
destination funnel.  The source-complete normal-Live word inequalities then
propagate the same metric until the next jump.  Induction over any finite hard
jump sequence proves domain safety and the post-jump practical-ISS bound.
\end{proof}

\subsection{Regional gravity-only certification on the detectable yaw quotient}
\label{sec:hybrid-quotient-capture}

The gravity-only symmetry acts on the complete estimator representation.  Let
$\mat T_\alpha$ be the tangent action induced by a horizontal rotation
$R_z(\alpha)$: it rotates the attitude/world coordinates consistently, rotates
$(v,p,S,a_w)$, leaves body-frame bias coordinates unchanged, and maps covariance
by congruence,
\begin{equation}
 \mat P\mapsto\mat T_\alpha\mat P\mat T_\alpha^\top.
 \label{eq:hybrid-quotient-covariance-action}
\end{equation}
Scalar schedules and enable flags are unchanged.  Denote this action on the
complete state/mode pair by $\mathcal G_\alpha(e,\pi)$ and its orbit by
$[(e,\pi)]$.  This removes the horizontal attitude gauge, but it does not make
the body-frame gyro-bias component parallel to gravity observable.

Let $\vct u_g$ be the predicted unit gravity direction in body coordinates and
split gyro-bias error into
\begin{equation}
 \delta\vct b_{g,\perp}:=\mat\Pi_g\delta\vct b_g,
 \qquad b_{g,\parallel}:=\vct u_g^\top\delta\vct b_g,
 \qquad \mat\Pi_g:=\mat I-\vct u_g\vct u_g^\top.
 \label{eq:hybrid-quotient-bias-split}
\end{equation}
A zero-rate gravity-only execution with
$\delta\vct b_g=b_{g,\parallel}\vct u_g$ produces only yaw.  Quotienting that
yaw therefore leaves $b_{g,\parallel}$ unchanged.  The computer-assisted source
audit verifies this exact zero dynamics and also verifies that the corresponding
covariance receives positive gyro-bias process noise.  Consequently a metric
that quotients yaw but still assigns a strict positive contraction weight to
$b_{g,\parallel}$ cannot satisfy a uniform $\lambda<1$ word inequality.  The
parallel bias is not declared a symmetry; it is a neutral/detectability input
until gravity-direction excitation or a magnetic gauge makes it observable.

Write the full source information metric in coordinates
$z=(z_d,b_{g,\parallel})$, after minimizing over horizontal gauge, as
\begin{equation}
 \mat M_i^\perp=
 \begin{bmatrix}
   \mat A_i^\perp&\vct B_i^\perp\\
   (\vct B_i^\perp)^\top&C_i^\parallel
 \end{bmatrix},
 \qquad C_i^\parallel>0.
\end{equation}
The detectable Schur metric is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 W_{i,d}^\perp([(e,\pi)])
 :=\inf_{\alpha\in[-\pi,\pi)}\inf_{\nu\in\mathbb R}
 W_i\!\left(\mathcal G_\alpha(e,\pi)+\nu E_\parallel\right)
 =z_d^\top\!\left(
 \mat A_i^\perp-
 \frac{\vct B_i^\perp(\vct B_i^\perp)^\top}{C_i^\parallel}
 \right)z_d .}
 \label{eq:hybrid-quotient-metric}
\end{equation}
Here the auxiliary minimization over $\nu$ is a Schur-complement elimination,
not an assertion that different axial gyro biases are physically equivalent.
It removes the neutral coordinate only from the strict Lyapunov seminorm while
retaining its coupling as an input to the detectable dynamics.

For an accepted gravity packet suppose
\begin{equation}
 \vct f_b=-g\vct u_g+\vct\epsilon_q,
 \qquad \|\vct\epsilon_q\|\le\bar f_q<g.
 \label{eq:hybrid-quotient-gravity-packet}
\end{equation}
Then $f_-:=g-\bar f_q>0$ and the cosine between
$-\vct f_b/\|f_b\|$ and $\vct u_g$ is at least
$c_q:=(g-\bar f_q)/(g+\bar f_q)>0$.  For every tangent tilt vector
$x\perp\vct u_g$,
\begin{equation}
 x^\top[\vct f_b]_\times^\top[\vct f_b]_\times x
 \ge f_-^2c_q^2\|x\|^2.
 \label{eq:hybrid-quotient-tilt-information}
\end{equation}
Thus one accepted packet is coercive on the two-dimensional tilt quotient.  Two
accepted packets separated by
$\Delta_q\in[\Delta_{q,-},\Delta_{q,+}]$ expose the transverse gyro-bias by the
same exact skew-transport argument used in
Lemma~\ref{lem:widen-two-packet-bg}.  If
$\bar\omega\Delta_{q,+}<2$, then
\begin{equation}
 \gamma_{q,-}:=\frac{\Delta_{q,-}}{T_{bg}}
 \left(1-\frac12\bar\omega\Delta_{q,+}\right)>0,
 \qquad
 \alpha_{4,q}:=
 \frac{f_-^2c_q^2/r_{a,+}}{1+2/\gamma_{q,-}^2}>0.
 \label{eq:hybrid-quotient-detectability}
\end{equation}
This is the reduced four-state $(\theta_\perp,b_{g,\perp})$ information bound.
The complete $(v,p,S,a_w)$ coordinates remain in the same source word and use
the already-certified four-$S$ translational qualification; they are not
removed from the quotient certificate.

In gravity-only mode, exact prediction, covariance propagation, accelerometer
correction, $S=0$ correction, quaternion reset, and the scalar source schedule
commute with the horizontal gauge action.  The exact source-word map therefore
descends to a well-defined quotient map $\mathcal F_w^\perp$.  The strict
funnel recursion is imposed only on the detectable Schur metric.  For every
source-complete gravity-only word require
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 W_{j,d}^\perp(\mathcal F_w^\perp([e],d))
 \le\lambda_{w,d}^\perp W_{i,d}^\perp([e])
 +\gamma_{w,\parallel}^\perp |b_{g,\parallel}|^2
 +\gamma_{w,d}^\perp(\bar d),
 \qquad \lambda_{w,d}^\perp<1.}
 \label{eq:hybrid-quotient-word}
\end{equation}
The same source-complete funnel recursion and prefix-safety requirement apply to
the detectable quotient nodes.  No strict contraction of
$b_{g,\parallel}$ is assumed.

\begin{theorem}[Regional gravity-only detectable source-funnel stability modulo yaw]
\label{thm:hybrid-quotient-capture}
Suppose the compact quotient handoff family $\mathcal H^\perp$ initializes
certified detectable funnel levels, the accepted gravity-packet recurrence
satisfies Eqs.~\eqref{eq:hybrid-quotient-gravity-packet}--
\eqref{eq:hybrid-quotient-detectability}, and
Eq.~\eqref{eq:hybrid-quotient-word} holds on a source-complete quotient word
family.  If $|b_{g,\parallel}|\le\bar b_\parallel$ on the deterministic quotient
interval, then gravity-only Live operation is regionally practically ISS on the
detectable quotient coordinates.  With
$\lambda_{B,d}^\perp:=\max_w\lambda_{w,d}^\perp<1$ and finite source-uniform
input coefficients,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 W_{n,d}^\perp
 \le(\lambda_{B,d}^\perp)^nW_{0,d}^\perp
 +\frac{1-(\lambda_{B,d}^\perp)^n}{1-\lambda_{B,d}^\perp}
 \left(
   \gamma_{B,\parallel}^\perp\bar b_\parallel^2
   +\gamma_{B,d}^\perp(\bar d)
 \right).}
 \label{eq:hybrid-quotient-practical}
\end{equation}
No convergence of absolute yaw is asserted, and no convergence of the neutral
axial gyro-bias component is asserted before additional excitation or magnetic
regauging makes that direction observable.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Equivariance makes the horizontal-gauge quotient word map independent of the
chosen yaw representative.  Schur-complement elimination removes the axial
bias only from the strict metric; its actual value remains in the source state
and is charged by the explicit input term in
Eq.~\eqref{eq:hybrid-quotient-word}.  The packet bound
Eq.~\eqref{eq:hybrid-quotient-detectability} supplies strict information on the
transverse attitude/bias coordinates, while the four-$S$ source word supplies
the translational qualification.  Iterating the resulting source-complete
funnel recursion gives Eq.~\eqref{eq:hybrid-quotient-practical}.
\end{proof}

If magnetic north is acquired after an ungauged Live handoff, the magnetic jump
selects one horizontal representative and changes the source mode from quotient
to full-heading operation.  The full-heading chain resumes exactly when the
jump satisfies Eq.~\eqref{eq:hybrid-jump-entry} for a certified full-heading
destination node.  The magnetic event may then make the formerly axial bias
direction observable; the quotient proof does not claim that this happened
earlier.
